  "scope": [
    "Windows 3.12 project environment, native search library available. Independent, serial loopback listeners on ephemeral ports. No solver start or stop commands were sent.",
    "Instrumentation delegates every observed call. It counts successful read_json_shared decodes by file size, full Path.read_bytes reads of the two digest inputs by actual length, and native manifest reads by file size. Counts cover the named inputs only; they do not measure total OS disk I/O or all requests made by Python.",
    "Every normal response was JSON-decoded, validated against all four copied files, and tied to its installation. For the seven archive polls, the full JSON response was compared after removing only the per-process token and the deliberately different installation root. Strict solver-start verification was left outside this HTTP benchmark.",
    "The synthetic case was tested with an already large history on first launch and again on reopening. The pre-fix batch script returned failure on both calls despite one healthy listener serving valid full state. The candidate kept one listener and its security token."
  ],
  "reproduction": [
    "Use git archive on the four listed commits, each in its own project-relative audit directory. Copy the four named runtime snapshots, data/tiles.json and .native/{search-build.json,constraint_native_search.dll}. The local venv uses the project Python shim/cfg and its installed packages.",
    "From each isolated installation, run OpenDashboard.cmd -NoBrowser -Port <available temporary port>. GET /api/state, reopen with exactly the same command, GET /api/state four further times, atomically update only status.json, then GET /api/state twice. Inspect /api/identity once where supported. Shut down only the isolated server.",
    "For the stress case use 24000 archived-schema history records before launching. Run the same batch command twice, each followed by a full JSON GET. Distinguish the exit code from the liveness of the actual listener.",
    "From a checkout use python -m unittest test_r35_dashboard_reads test_platform for public automated regression coverage. The original owner-specific independent inputs and raw traces are retained locally under audit/r35/dashboard88-independent/.",
    "To exercise the legacy fallback, keep each v1.15.0 listener running, update only the launcher to the final commit in that installation, and reopen using the same batch command and port."
  ],
